title: SPIR-V Specification
author: John Kessenich, Google
author: Boaz Ouriel, Intel
changes:

=== Changes from Version 1.00, Revision 10

 - Add *HLSL* <<Source_Language, *source language*>>.
 - Add *StorageBuffer* <<Storage_Class, *storage class*>>.
 - Add *StorageBuffer16BitAccess*,  *UniformAndStorageBuffer16BitAccess*, *VariablePointersStorageBuffer*, and *VariablePointers* <<Capability, capabilities>>.
 - Khronos SPIR-V issue #163: Be more clear that <<OpTypeStruct, *OpTypeStruct*>> allows zero members.
   Also affects *ArrayStride* and *Offset* decoration <<Validation, validation rules>>.
 - Khronos SPIR-V issue #159: List allowed *AtomicCounter* instructions with the *AtomicStorage* <<Capability, capability>> rather than the validation rules.
 - Khronos SPIR-V issue #36: Describe more clearly the type of _ND Range_ in <<OpGetKernelNDrangeSubGroupCount, *OpGetKernelNDrangeSubGroupCount*>>,
   <<OpGetKernelNDrangeMaxSubGroupSize, *OpGetKernelNDrangeMaxSubGroupSize*>>, and <<OpEnqueueKernel, *OpEnqueueKernel*>>.
 - Khronos SPIR-V issue #128: Be clear the <<OpDot, *OpDot*>> operates only on vectors.
 - Khronos SPIR-V issue #80: Loop headers must dominate their continue target. See <<StructuredControlFlow, Structured Control Flow>>.
 - Khronos SPIR-V issue #150 allow *UniformConstant* <<Storage_Class, storage-class>> variables to have initializers, depending on the client API.
